      "problem": "Given $f(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+1}}{\\sqrt{x}},$ find $f(4).$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $4$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8+1}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
